          "text": "# Fix: the supersession marker can assert a re-bake that never happened\n\nYou are a builder fixing one correctness defect in code that is already committed and passing\nall gates. Another builder wrote it; you are repairing it, not continuing its lane.\n\nRepo: `/home/leon0399/.herdr/worktrees/llame/recent-chats-digest-in-prompt`\nBranch `recency-digest/compaction` (already checked out). Read `apps********S.md` first.\n\n**HARD RULE: never run any `git` command** — no commit, stash, checkout, reset, branch. The\norchestrating session owns version control. A `git stash` here destroys work that is not yours.\n\n## The defect\n\n`apps/api/src/chats/chat-loop.service.ts` decides whether to emit the digest supersession\nmarker like this:\n\n```ts\nconst digestRebaked =\n  activeCompaction !== undefined &&\n  previousRun !== undefined &&\n  activeCompaction.createdAt > previousRun.createdAt;\n...\nconst digestSupersessionPart =\n  digestRebaked && chat.recencyDigestBaseline !== null && shareRecentChats?.shareRecentChats === true\n    ? createRecencyDigestSupersessionPart({ runId: input.targetRunId })\n    : undefined;\n```\n\nThat derives \"a re-bake happened\" from \"a compaction happened since the last run\". Those are\nnot the same thing. In `apps/api/src/compaction/compaction.service.ts` the re-bake is\n**conditional**, while the compaction row is created unconditionally in the same transaction:\n\n```ts\nif (chat?.recencyDigestBaseline != null && digestCandidate !== null && shareRecentChats.shareRecentChats) {\n  await new ChatsRepository(tx).setRecencyDigest(...);\n}\nawait compactionsRepo.create({ ... });\n```\n\nSo the marker fires on the next turn even when no re-bake occurred. **Two reachable paths:**\n\n1. **Sharing disabled at compaction time, re-enabled before the next turn.** The re-bake is\n   correctly skipped (withdrawal is not retroactive), the compaction row lands, and the next\n   turn emits a marker.\n2. **`digestCandidate === null